
               STory CReator for DayDream BBS v1.26 & Above
              ----------------------------------------------
                                                By : Xpose



 Introduction
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~
 It has always been hell trying to find doors for Daydream BBS, and once you
find them you realise they aren't that "satisfactory", or they aren't exactly
what you need or had in mind .. Especially games doors, you can't find
anything special for DDBBS ... That's what brought me to create a few
interesting Doors for this great BBS program .. And as a result of a few
hours work, I managed to create this door, intitled STory CReator, or just
SToryC for short.

 The idea is very simple behind SToryC, all it does is creates a file, and
everybody writes a line as part of the story, every line added will be copied
to the story file (STory.ST), thus every user contributes a line or two for
the story. It's most enjoyable when you have a lot of users coming and going
on your BBS, especially when the users check the story out .



 Installation
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~
 I'm sorry in a way that I haven't managed to include an installation script
for SToryC, but what difference does it make, all you have to do is move both
"SToryC.dd" and "STory.ST" to your DOORS: directory, and then add a few lines
to your config file and et vuala !(I know NO French), I hope you have MUI,
becuase I can't remember what you are supposed to add in the config script,
if you do have MUI just add the door as a DayDream door and make sure the
execute cmd is something like this :

 DOORS:Rexx %N Doors:SToryC.dd

 Very simple. Also you can make it run everytime someone logs on (aka logon
door), by just adding the files destination to your Welcome.GFX file, you'll
find it in "Daydream:Display/iso/".



 Help
 ~~~~
 If you need any help just start your installation procedure again. Else,
contact the Author

 
 
 Author
 ~~~~~~
 Author ? Who ? Me ? Wow ! Oh well, I am a 15 (16 in Feb) year old high 
school student with a lot of time. A few months ago I downloaded Daydream BBS 
just to check it out, I downloaded it with a few other BBS proggies, but I 
tended to favour Daydream for its speed and configurability (wow, long word!),
soon I got the likes of it and began setting up my BBS . I didn't put it
online straight ahead, back then I didn't have a phoneline !! But I tested
the program and logged on locally, at sometimes my friends would check it out
when I get my hands on a modem for a day or two .. But once again, the BBS
never looked special because it never had a lot of good doors, you'd be
pretty bored if you just stayed on for a few minutes (one or two), and a lot
of my friends (PC users) told me that my bbs sucks because it doesn't have
enjoyable stuff, and kept on comparing it to other `Porffesional' BBSs
available online .. I survived the critisism, and headed to the store, bought
tons of food, came back home, locked myself in my castle, and hit it away
with experimintation . SToryC was the result of all that. After a few million
years (three or four hours), and after billions of Dr.Peppers (3 and two
Miranda Apples), and trillions of Maltesers(two I think ..) I came out of my
cosey room victorious !! I called up a few pals and showed off ! Soon I
showed it to an AMIGA fan, and he liked it. The rest is now history .

 I am planning to produce more stuff for Daydream BBS, I hope though that I
do get some support, a simple email will make my day ! So, any suggestions,
contributions (ANSI graphics mostly) will be MOSTLY accepted ! Or just drop
me a letter just to make friends . 


